  "question": "Does NCPSsd expose a stable anonymous first-party public search surface whose client controls can be inspected without using the NLC cooperation login bridge or guessing a search endpoint?",
  "answer": "Yes at the UI/control level, but the executable URL/parameter contract is not yet closed. The public https://www.ncpssd.cn/ and https://www.ncpssd.org/ roots each return HTTP 200 with the identical 198,008-byte object and identical SHA-256. The page exposes a basic search text input id=text_search, a button invoking Basicsearch(), hidden search-state inputs hidSearchType/hidSearchValue, hidden select_type with value TS, and advanced-search controls invoking AdvancedSearch(), Search_text(), qkSearchCondition(), Search_GJ() and waiwen_search(). There is no HTML form. External first-party scripts fetched in KH are generic libraries and do not close the Basicsearch execution contract, indicating the relevant search logic is likely inline in the homepage. No query is submitted.",
